---
import { CONTACT_EMAIL } from '@/constants';
import DefaultLayout from '@/layouts/DefaultLayout.astro';

const lastUpdated = 'October 16, 2026';
---

<DefaultLayout
  title="Privacy Policy | AtlasOS"
  description="AtlasOS privacy policy covering the website, analytics, the download counter, Atlas Manager reports, third-party services, and your rights."
>
  <section class="mx-auto mt-16 max-w-4xl px-4 pb-16">
    <h1 class="mb-2 text-4xl font-semibold tracking-tight text-white md:text-5xl">Privacy Policy</h1>
    <p class="mb-8 text-sm text-white/50">Last updated: {lastUpdated}</p>

    <div class="space-y-8 leading-relaxed text-white/75">
      <div>
        <h2 class="mb-3 text-xl font-semibold text-white">Overview</h2>
        <p>
          AtlasOS is an open-source project that modifies Windows to improve performance, privacy, and usability. We
          keep data collection to a minimum and explain here exactly what we do process. This policy covers the AtlasOS
          website (<strong class="text-white/90">atlasos.net</strong>), the services it uses, and the AtlasOS software
          including Atlas Manager. The bot of the AtlasOS Discord server has{' '}
          <a class="text-primary hover:underline" href="/privacy-policy/discord-bot/">
            its own privacy policy
          </a>
          .
        </p>
      </div>

      <div>
        <h2 class="mb-3 text-xl font-semibold text-white">Website Analytics</h2>
        <p>
          We measure website traffic with{' '}
          <a class="text-primary hover:underline" href="https://plausible.io" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">
            Plausible Analytics
          </a>{' '}
          Community Edition, which we host ourselves at <strong class="text-white/90">pla.atlasos.net</strong>. It does
          not use cookies and does not track you across websites. To count unique visitors, Plausible combines your IP
          address and browser user agent with a random value that changes every 24 hours and keeps only the resulting
          one-way identifier; your IP address is used to look up your country and is never stored. We see aggregate
          statistics such as page views, referring sites, browser, operating system, and country. The data stays on our
          own server and is not shared with Plausible or anyone else.
        </p>
      </div>

      <div>
        <h2 class="mb-3 text-xl font-semibold text-white">Download Counter</h2>
        <p class="mb-3">
          When you click a download button, the website tells our download counter at{' '}
          <strong class="text-white/90">api.atlasos.net</strong> that a download happened. So that each visitor is
          counted once per version, the counter stores a one-way hash of your IP address combined with the version and a
          secret key. Your IP address itself is not stored, and the counter keeps no logs of it. The hashes are kept so
          that repeat downloads are not counted twice.
        </p>
        <p>
          The homepage also shows how many people starred AtlasOS on GitHub and the public GitHub names and avatars of
          recent stargazers, which our server copies from GitHub's public API.
        </p>
      </div>

      <div>
        <h2 class="mb-3 text-xl font-semibold text-white">AI Documentation Assistant</h2>
        <p>
          Our documentation includes an optional AI assistant provided by{' '}
          <a class="text-primary hover:underline" href="https://kapa.ai" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">
            Kapa.ai
          </a>
          . It only loads when you open it. Your questions and the conversation are sent to Kapa.ai to generate answers,
          and Kapa.ai protects the assistant against abuse with Google reCAPTCHA, so Google also receives information
          about your browser while you use it. See{' '}
          <a
            class="text-primary hover:underline"
            href="https://www.kapa.ai/privacy-policy"
            target="_blank"
            rel="noopener noreferrer"
          >
            Kapa.ai's privacy policy
          </a>{' '}
          and{' '}
          <a
            class="text-primary hover:underline"
            href="https://policies.google.com/privacy"
            target="_blank"
            rel="noopener noreferrer"
          >
            Google's privacy policy
          </a>
          .
        </p>
      </div>

      <div>
        <h2 class="mb-3 text-xl font-semibold text-white">Windows ISO Downloads</h2>
        <p>
          The Windows download tool in our documentation asks our Cloudflare Worker for official download links. The
          Worker retrieves them from Microsoft and caches the links (and nothing about you) for up to 24 hours. The ISO
          file itself downloads directly from Microsoft, which receives your IP address under{' '}
          <a
            class="text-primary hover:underline"
            href="https://privacy.microsoft.com/privacystatement"
            target="_blank"
            rel="noopener noreferrer"
          >
            Microsoft's privacy statement
          </a>
          . Cloudflare keeps short-lived technical logs of requests to the Worker for troubleshooting.
        </p>
      </div>

      <div>
        <h2 class="mb-3 text-xl font-semibold text-white">Other Services Your Browser Contacts</h2>
        <p>
          Some pages load release information directly from GitHub's API, and download buttons and links lead to GitHub
          (Atlas releases), Ameliorated (AME Wizard), jsDelivr (brand assets), and Microsoft. When your browser connects
          to these services, they receive your IP address and process it under their own privacy policies.
        </p>
      </div>

      <div>
        <h2 class="mb-3 text-xl font-semibold text-white">Cookies</h2>
        <p>
          This website does not set any cookies of its own, and our analytics work without cookies. Cloudflare may set a
          strictly necessary security cookie when it checks whether a visitor is a bot, and the AI assistant may store
          data in your browser while you use it. We do not use advertising or tracking cookies.
        </p>
      </div>

      <div>
        <h2 class="mb-3 text-xl font-semibold text-white">Data We Do Not Collect</h2>
        <ul class="list-disc space-y-1 pl-6">
          <li>The website does not ask for your name or email address, and we do not store visitors' IP addresses.</li>
          <li>We do not use cookies or local storage to track you, and we do not track you across websites.</li>
          <li>We do not sell, rent, or share any data with third parties for advertising or marketing.</li>
          <li>We do not build profiles of visitors.</li>
        </ul>
      </div>

      <div>
        <h2 class="mb-3 text-xl font-semibold text-white">AtlasOS Software</h2>
        <p class="mb-3">
          AtlasOS runs entirely on your PC and has no telemetry. Atlas Manager connects on its own only to GitHub, to
          check for and download Atlas releases, and to Microsoft's Windows release information page. It identifies
          itself to them as Atlas Manager, and they receive your IP address. All source code is publicly available on{' '}
          <a
            class="text-primary hover:underline"
            href="https://github.com/Atlas-OS/Atlas"
            target="_blank"
            rel="noopener noreferrer"
          >
            GitHub
          </a>
          .
        </p>
        <p>
          Nothing is sent to us unless you choose <strong class="text-white/90">Send a report</strong> in Atlas Manager
          or use the report website at <strong class="text-white/90">reports.atlasos.net</strong>. A report contains
          your message, any contact details you choose to give, the Atlas Manager version, and any diagnostics you
          include; you can review the diagnostics before sending. Reports are visible only to the Atlas team. The team
          may use AI services from other companies to help investigate; these receive your message and diagnostics but
          never your contact details. Reports, and any copies the team downloads, are deleted after 90 days. The report
          service's security systems may record connection details, including IP addresses.
        </p>
      </div>

      <div>
        <h2 class="mb-3 text-xl font-semibold text-white">Email</h2>
        <p>
          If you email us, we receive your email address and message. Cloudflare Email Routing forwards them to the
          team, and we use them only to reply to you.
        </p>
      </div>

      <div>
        <h2 class="mb-3 text-xl font-semibold text-white">Hosting &amp; Security</h2>
        <p>
          The website is hosted on{' '}
          <a
            class="text-primary hover:underline"
            href="https://www.cloudflare.com"
            target="_blank"
            rel="noopener noreferrer"
          >
            Cloudflare
          </a>
          . Our analytics, download counter and status page run on a server operated by AtlasOS that is reachable only
          through Cloudflare, with its data encrypted at rest. Cloudflare processes technical data such as IP addresses
          to deliver the site and protect it from attacks; see{' '}
          <a
            class="text-primary hover:underline"
            href="https://www.cloudflare.com/privacypolicy/"
            target="_blank"
            rel="noopener noreferrer"
          >
            Cloudflare's privacy policy
          </a>
          . All of our sites are served only over HTTPS.
        </p>
      </div>

      <div>
        <h2 class="mb-3 text-xl font-semibold text-white">Your Rights</h2>
        <p>
          You can ask us what data we hold about you, or ask us to correct or delete it, by emailing us. Website
          analytics cannot be linked back to you. For a report you sent, tell us roughly when you sent it and any
          contact details you gave so we can find it. We respond within 30 days.
        </p>
      </div>

      <div>
        <h2 class="mb-3 text-xl font-semibold text-white">Children's Privacy</h2>
        <p>
          This website is not directed at children under the age of 13. We do not knowingly collect any personal
          information from children.
        </p>
      </div>

      <div>
        <h2 class="mb-3 text-xl font-semibold text-white">Changes to This Policy</h2>
        <p>
          We will update this policy when we start processing something new or use data differently. The date at the top
          always shows the latest version.
        </p>
      </div>

      <div>
        <h2 class="mb-3 text-xl font-semibold text-white">Contact</h2>
        <p>
          If you have questions about this privacy policy, contact us at
          <a class="text-primary hover:underline" href={`mailto:${CONTACT_EMAIL}`}>
            {CONTACT_EMAIL}
          </a>
          .
        </p>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>
</DefaultLayout>
